  "overview": {
    "title": "Village and wild water",
    "p1": "Cala Iris is a small fishing settlement and cove along the national park coast — a clear step away from Al Hoceima’s urban beaches into a quieter Rif Mediterranean shoreline.",
    "p2": "The draw is the setting: boats, clear water and cliffs rather than city services. It works well as the anchor of a park-coast day with a driver or organised transfer.",
    "p3": "Bring what you need for sun and swimming. Facilities are limited compared with Quemado or Sfiha."
